# The DB-bundled OCI client's AUTH Phase 1 (sqlplus 23.26, from
# gvenzl/oracle-free:23-slim), captured whole against a dbbat proxy. TNS Data
# payload: two data-flag bytes, then the TTC message.
#
# It opens with the same 64-bit op header its proxy-mode frames use:
#
#   03 76 02 00 00 <ub4 0> <sb8 3 = seq+1> fe(x8)
#
# The Instant Client 23.3 writes `03 76 02 01 03 fe(x8)` here -- five bytes
# where this one writes seventeen. That difference is the only evidence a
# session has of which summary object to write before its first upstream OER
# arrives, which is why it is pinned rather than inferred.
#
# The AUTH_ keys further in are what payloadUsesWideKVEncoding reads, so the
# whole packet is kept: both dialect flags are asserted off this one fixture.

